A||N||5||GT-maniac||Oil pressure sender||||5||
Z||000000||GT-maniac||05-19-2000||10:11 PM||||Well went under my car today to find out why the oil pressure gauge wasn't working. Found the sender wiring just hanging there not connected to anything. I saw the sending units hole which is plugged with a metal plug. So I bought sending unit ( pretty pricey sender ). Problem is I can't get the damn thing in ! It's so wide that it rubs on some piece of the motor by the oil filter and won't go in. The only solution that I can see is to use some brass piping and fittings to extend the hole the sender fits into out far enough for the sender to clear the obstruction. My question is why would I have to do this to install a stock sensor on a stock 2.8 engine ? Anybody else have problems with this ? ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Linx||05-19-2000||10:49 PM||||i think you're missing some hardware...<P>My 2.8 has a length of tubing that runs from that hole, up past the exhaust manifold, ac compressor and coolant hoses, and allows the sensor to be mounted on the front of the engine, to the right of the water pump.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Linx||05-20-2000||02:31 AM||||I looked around and found this pic I took during my rebuild- it shows the tubing.  The top end of the tube ends in a small threaded block that accepts the oil pressure sensor.<P>  <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/linxramblr/oiltube.jpg">   <P><p>[This message has been edited by Linx (edited 05-20-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Phaeton||05-20-2000||11:37 AM||||And a loose wobbly piece of extention it is, at least on my 2.8.  Had a mech friend blame it on no advance planning to fit AC in the Fiero, don't know, never seen a Fiero without AC (OK, I haven't seen many Fiero's).||||reg||1
Z||000004||GT-maniac||05-20-2000||08:14 PM||||Thanks for the replies guys, I guess I'll have to find that tube somewhere, maybe the dealer. BTW I must be one of the unlucky few without air conditioning, or cruise control or power locks. Ah well can't have everything I guess||||reg||7
Z||000005||triker||05-22-2000||12:15 PM||||When I removed the Air on my trike, it left the oil sender hanging in mid air, and a bolt missing from the dogbone mounting plate.  I used a long stud and 3 nuts to secure everything back in place.||||reg||1
